      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks wrong.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day. The usual maximum is about 2550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets (some references allow 3000 mg/day) and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. The 5100 mg/day total is roughly double that ceiling, even though this patient has normal kidney and liver function. Metformin is also not commonly dispensed as 1700 mg tablets; immediate-release strengths are typically 500, 850, and 1000 mg.\n\nSome possibilities:\n- **850 mg TID** (2550 mg/day), a common maximum regimen\n- **1000 mg BID** (2000 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg BID** (3400 mg/day), if you intended a higher total and have a reason for it\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose, frequency, and formulation (immediate or extended release), and I'll enter the order. If 5100 mg/day is intentional, please confirm that too, and I can add a note documenting the rationale."
      }
