       "type": "text",
       "text": "I entered the order as written: metformin 1700 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (Order ID: ORD-0001).\n\nThe total daily dose is 5100 mg, which is well above the usual maximum of about 2550\u20133000 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. I added a note to the order recording that the dose exceeds the usual maximum, that you confirmed it as written, and that pharmacist review is requested.\n\nPlease check the dose with pharmacy and the patient's current labs and clinical status. Metformin at high doses raises the risk of lactic acidosis, and 1700 mg tablets are not a standard strength, so the dispensed product and tablet count need to be clear. If the dose was not intended, the order can be changed or discontinued in the order-entry system."
